-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T22:33:11-07:00","id":1153065,"title":"","content":"-<b>p. 21</b> &quot;You pray. You work. <i><b>you...rest</b></i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> The &quot;<i>you...</i>&quot; should be capitalized.<br /> <br /> Should read as &quot;You pray. You work. You...rest.&quot;<br /> <br /> -<b>p. 22</b> &quot;...didn\u2019t want the fog of <i><b>glamour</b></i> to make him lie in the booth.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;glamour&quot; should be capitalized.<br /> <br /> Should read as &quot;...didn't want the fog of Glamour to make him lie in the booth.&quot;<br /> <br /> -<b>p. 27 </b>&quot; 'and if they move against her they're no better than a pack of loyalist dogs. &quot;<br /> <br /> There is a missing quotation mark after &quot;dogs.&quot;<br /> <br /> Should read as &quot; 'and if they move against her they're no better than a pack of loyalist dogs.' &quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 10-26-2017, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T12:39:15-07:00","id":1153566,"title":"","content":"<b>-p. 48</b> &quot;The <b>hedge</b> had pulled and torn at him.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;After the <b>hedge</b>, in the hospital, Brian was at peace.&quot;<br /> <br /> In both instances &quot;hedge&quot; should be capitalized. Should read as:<br /> <br /> &quot;The Hedge had pulled and torn at him.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;After the Hedge, in the hospital, Brian was at peace.&quot;<br /> <br /> -<b>p.50 </b>&quot;When I sleep, I the chant of <b>' '</b> 'champion' haunting my dreams.&quot;<br /> <br /> There is a pair of extraneous quotation marks in front of &quot;champion&quot;.<br /> <br /> Should read as:<br /> <br /> &quot;When I sleep, I the chant of 'champion' haunting my dreams.&quot;<br /> <br /> -<b>p. 74 </b>&quot;<b>Let</b> him alone, and many flee, but none are saved.&quot;<br /> <br /> Awkward wording, replace &quot;Let&quot; with &quot;Leave&quot;.<br /> <br /> Should read as &quot;Leave him alone, and many flee, but none are saved.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T12:20:22-07:00","id":1153779,"title":"","content":"-<b>p. 83</b> &quot;...after discovering their <b>huntman</b> softly breathing the same stale air.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;huntman&quot; is both a misspelling of &quot;huntsman&quot; and needs to be capitalized.<br /> <br /> Should read as: &quot;...after discovering their Huntsman softly breathing the same stale air.&quot;<br /> <br /> -<b>p. 84 </b>&quot;'They're only <b>kindof</b> real here.'&quot;<br /> <br /> There's a space missing in between &quot;kind&quot; and &quot;of&quot;.<br /> <br /> Should read as &quot;'They're only kind of real here.'&quot;<br /> <br /> -<b>p. 95 </b>&quot;As <b>the</b> talked...&quot;<br /> <br /> This is a misspelling of &quot;they&quot;.<br /> <br /> Should read as &quot;As they talked...&quot;<br /> <br /> -<b>p. 103 </b>&quot;I'm supposed to make a joke <b>her</b> about a woman's drawers...&quot;<br /> <br /> This is a misspelling of &quot;here&quot;.<br /> <br /> This should read as &quot;I'm supposed to make a joke here about a woman's drawers...&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T13:38:31-07:00","id":1155510,"title":"","content":"As always, I greatly appreciate the work that Onyx Path does and I'm so glad we fans can to contribute to making these books even better.<br /> <br /> I'm noticing a ton of question marks in Broken Things. Some seem like they were meant to be other punctuation, but other times I think it's the author's style or character's voice, or maybe an error of how the text was encoded. Anyway, here's what I found.<br /> <br /> <u>Confusing Question Mark</u> - p. 16 &quot;Now? He stared at a statue..&quot; I didn't think this was an error when I first read it, but now I'm not so sure it wasn't meant to be a comma.<br /> <br /> <u>Replaced Comma x2 &amp; Unnecessary Carriage Return</u> - p. 16 &quot;Bereft of hard-earned answers? He knelt and prayed. And, as he submitted himself?&quot; 1st '?' should be a comma because the beginning is a dependent clause. The &quot;And&quot; clause is a sentence fragment caused by the second '?' followed by a carriage return that shouldn't be there.<br /> <br /> <u>Confusing Question Mark</u> - p. 16 &quot;Taking its shape? Familiar.&quot; Again, I didn't think this was wrong on the first read, but maybe it was supposed to be something else.<br /> <br /> <u>Replaced Comma</u> - p.17 &quot;After the overnights crawled out the door? He made fresh coffee.&quot; The question mark is pretty clearly supposed to be a comma.<br /> <br /> <u>Unnecessary Comma &amp; Replaced Comma</u> - p. 17 - &quot;Once you know, what you can do? Thinking only makes it worse.&quot; The comma isn't separating two clauses and I suspect the '?' was meant to be a comma.<br /> <br /> <u>Missing Comma</u> - p. 17 &quot;...dripped and steamed but he had a pot done and a mug in his palms.&quot; Comma needed before &quot;but&quot; and possibly before the &quot;and a mug in his palms.&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Missing Comma</u> - p. 17 &quot;...those blossoms, thin white razors...&quot; A pair of adjectives like &quot;thin&quot; and &quot;white&quot; need a comma or conjunction.<br /> <br /> <u>Another Question Mark</u> - p. 17 &quot;But as the small pond started to go stale? So too did the fish.&quot; The pond clause is definitely dependent and probably needs a comma to attach it to the second clause.<br /> <br /> <u>Confusing Question Mark</u> - p. 18 &quot;Now? He felt a little guilty about it&quot; This can pass, but in light of the other unusual question marks, I wonder if this might be another comma in disguise.<br /> <br /> <u>Replaced Comma</u> - p. 18 &quot;After electronics? He enjoyed most of his lunch&quot; Pretty clear the '?' should be a ','<br /> <br /> <u>Confusing Question Mark</u> - p. 18 &quot;She? Didn\u2019t feel a thing.&quot; Shouldn't be a comma, but maybe this was intention considering the list of tense questions 2 lines above it. It's hard to see the line between the author's voice and the errors.<br /> <br /> <u>Replaced Comma &amp; Unnecessary Carriage Return</u> - p. 18 &quot;To him?[ ]She was a shadow&quot; Similar to p. 16, this is a comma masquerading as a &quot;?&quot; and a paragraph break.<br /> <br /> <u>Replaced Comma</u> - p. 18 &quot;After lunch? Rounds and hardware.&quot; Question mark should be a comma. &quot;rounds and hardware&quot; isn't an independent clause, technically, but it fits in its context.<br /> <br /> <u>Commas?</u> - p. 18 &quot;...the bigger, bolder 24-hour behemoth store.&quot; Most of these are adjectives and so it should read &quot;the bigger, bolder, 24-hour, behemoth store.&quot;, though one can also argue that &quot;24-hour behemoth store&quot; is one solid noun.<br /> <br /> <u>Replaced Comma</u> - p. 18 &quot;After that? He locked up.&quot; Another question mark in place of a comma.<br /> <br /> <u>Replaced Comma</u> - p. 18 &quot;So, after all of that? He slipped out through...&quot; See, when it's every other paragraph, I start wondering if it was an accident.<br /> <br /> <u>Replaced Comma</u> - p. 19 &quot;First? It had to learn the land.&quot; What's weird here is that we had a shift in perspective to something old and supernatural, but strangely it writes with the same constantly questioning structure that Corwyn does? Using the same style for both eats away at the sense of contrast and the otherworldliness of this thing inhabiting the priest. I mean, for Corwyn, it gives the reader a sense of his own nagging uncertainty, which he tries to keep at bay through &quot;grinding.&quot; Meanwhile, the uncertainty betrayed by the question marks seems out of character for a being repeatedly pained by the mutability of our existence. I'm probably way off. Sorry for the ramble. <br /> <br /> <u>Commas?</u> p.19 &quot;haunted people. Which ones were safe. Which ones were sacred.&quot; Technically, these need commas not periods, but it's also an author's voice thing too, in this case.<br /> <br /> <u>Replaced Comma</u> - p. 20 &quot;And as it had expected? What was needed was delivered...&quot; Comma in place of the question mark.<br /> <br /> <u>Unnecessary Question and Capitalization</u> - p. 21 &quot;Those who live and die? Live through a calculus of minor sins.&quot; The phrase &quot;Those who live and die?&quot; is not a complete sentence. Neither is &quot;Live through a calculus of minor sins.&quot; unless it's being used as a command, which has an implied subject. I suspect that this is supposed to just be a single, observational sentence instead of anything fancy<br /> <br /> <u>Replaced Comma</u> - p. 21 &quot;...practice made perfect. So? He stopped trying.&quot; Comma in place of the question mark.<br /> <br /> <u>Missing word</u> - p. 21 &quot;He thought other people in impossible places.&quot; This needs an &quot;of&quot; or &quot;about&quot; between &quot;thought&quot; and &quot;other people&quot;.<br /> <br /> <u>Replaced Comma</u> - p. 22 &quot;With practice? Maybe he could handle it.&quot; Needs a comma in place of the question mark.<br /> <br /> <u>Odd Phrasing</u> - p. 22 &quot;He felt warm red before the cut had time to sting.&quot; I found &quot;warm red&quot; to feel awkward, but I'm not sure how to adjust it. I guess you could replace &quot;warm red&quot; with &quot;blood&quot; but that's not as cool sounding. Maybe &quot;warm blood&quot;? Maybe just leave it?<br /> <br /> <u>Adverb/Adjective Conjugation</u> - p. 22 &quot;I am here to bring a love and faith and struggle eternally to one who can appreciate the beauty of eternal things.&quot; In this case, I think &quot;struggle eternally&quot; should be &quot;eternal struggle&quot; or, to sound appropriately priest-like, &quot;struggle eternal.&quot; (Also, there's a list with multiple 'and's that should use a comma, but it kinda sounds cooler how it is.)<br /> <br /> <u>Replaced Comma</u> - p. 22 &quot;On its lips? The word dripped,&quot; Definitely should be a comma instead of a question mark.<br /> <br /> <u>Replaced Comma</u> - p. 22 &quot;...the lesser and the lies? You reveled.&quot; We've got 2 great dependent clauses and need a comma, not a question mark, to join them to the independent &quot;You reveled.&quot;<br /> <br /> <u>Replaced Comma</u> - p. 23 &quot;But then? Corwyn surprised them both.&quot; Change the question mark to a comma.<br /> <br /> <u>Replaced Comma</u> - p. 23 &quot;...rest of the stories? The end is one long...&quot; You know the drill<br /> <br /> <u>Weird phrasing &amp; punctuation</u> - p. 23 &quot;Where I go? Everything awaits. Feel everything? Perhaps self will be among the seasons.&quot; The first of these question marks should probably be a comma. I'm really not sure how &quot;Feel everything?&quot; really fits into the passage; it doesn't seem like it was supposed to be a stand-alone question or a dependent clause. Should &quot;Feel everything&quot; just have a period, so that it becomes sort of a command? I'm sad to say not sure what is being meant here.<br /> <br /> Uncapitalizing will be needed along with most of these '?' to ',' changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1925,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1925-toroid","user":"Toroid","date":". 11-07-2017, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1925-toroid","name":"Toroid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}